VERDICT: FAIL
CHECKER: checker-a11y
FAMILY: anthropic
TASK: U13
ATTEMPT: 1
---
SCOPE: uncommitted diff on feat/ui-audit (HEAD 5bfc4c8) vs `command git diff`
(NOT `git diff master`, which also includes prior committed U-run tasks).
Touched: healthcare-person.html, income-card.html, income-sources-list.html,
quick-adjust.html, whatif.html, whatif-income-toast.js (new), plus a Go
handler test (handlers_test.go). Rendered live via
`scripts/whatif-verify.sh start 8092` (isolated `cp -rL` data copy) and
inspected with curl + a real Chromium via Playwright, axe-core 4.13.0
injected into the live-rendered DOM (not hand-built HTML). Server stopped
at the end of the audit.

====================================================================
FAILURE — decisive, reproduces on a completely fresh isolated copy
====================================================================

Constitution: ACCESSIBILITY.md #14 ("Banners ... are re-announced only on
state change, not every page load within a session") and the task's own
acceptance line (U-RUN-SPEC.md §2g / ledger row U13(b)): "On initial page
load the toast is not shown (a past-session removal must not resurface)."
Also implicates WCAG 2.2 4.1.3 Status Messages (a role="status" region's
content must correspond to what actually just happened).

File: web/templates/components/whatif/income-sources-list.html, the
`whatif-removed-income-sources` define block (this task's own rewrite of
that block — not pre-existing markup; `git diff` confirms it's new for
this attempt).

Observed behavior (reproduced twice, once on a server already exercised by
my own probes, once on a server freshly restarted from a clean `cp -rL`
copy so it could not be attributed to my own test actions):

1. Fresh server start. `data/settings/whatif.json` (the real production
   plan, isolated-copied) already has 5 entries in `removed_income_sources`
   accumulated from PAST sessions (Christine Job, Christine Pension,
   Christine, Rebuild Payroll x2) — this is real, current plan state, not
   test fixture noise.
2. GET /whatif (initial load): toast placeholder correctly renders hidden,
   empty (`<div id="income-removed-toast" class="hidden" role="status">`).
   This part of the fix works.
3. First mutating action of the session — PUT
   /whatif/healthcare/{id} (an unrelated healthcare-coverage edit, nothing
   to do with income sources) — response includes an hx-swap-oob fragment:
     <div id="income-removed-toast" hx-swap-oob="true" role="status"
         class="fixed bottom-6 ... (no `hidden` class)">
       <span>Removed <span class="font-medium">Rebuild Payroll</span></span>
       <button ... data-income-toast-undo>Undo</button>
       <button ... data-income-toast-dismiss aria-label="Dismiss">...</button>
     </div>
   i.e. a VISIBLE, `role="status"` toast announcing "Removed Rebuild
   Payroll" pops up in response to an action that removed nothing —
   Rebuild Payroll was removed in some past session. Reproduced identically
   on a second, unrelated healthcare PUT (a different person's coverage).

Root cause: `whatif-removed-income-sources` is included, unconditionally,
inside the `whatif-results` OOB template block that EVERY mutating
what-if handler re-renders (htmx targets `#whatif-results` from ~all
controls on the page: healthcare edits, quick-adjust sliders, phases,
scenario switches, etc. — confirmed via `grep -c hx-target="#whatif-results"`
across the page templates). The template picks "the last entry of
RemovedIncomeSources" and renders it un-hidden whenever the list is
non-empty, with no way to distinguish "an item was just removed by THIS
request" from "the list has old debris nobody purged" (the old permanent
list supported per-item purge; this task deleted the purge button/affordance
along with the list, so there is no longer any UI path to clear old
entries — they now persist and keep re-triggering the toast forever).

Consequence for assistive-technology users: a `role="status"` (implicit
aria-live="polite") live region fires a false "Removed X. Undo." on
essentially every interaction with the /whatif page for as long as any
stale RemovedIncomeSources entries exist in the plan — which they
currently do, in the real plan file. This is exactly the "junk text
injected via a live region" class of defect called out in my audit
instructions, and it is the general-case version of the very failure mode
the task's own acceptance criterion 1 was written to prevent ("a past-
session removal must not resurface") — it just resurfaces on the first
click instead of on page load, which is worse (page load is a single
event; this fires on every subsequent mutation too).

Reproduction commands (isolated port, no live-data risk):
  scripts/whatif-verify.sh start 8092
  curl -s localhost:8092/whatif | grep -A1 'id="income-removed-toast"'
    # hidden, empty — correct
  HID=$(curl -s localhost:8092/whatif | grep -o 'hx-put="/whatif/healthcare/[^"]*"' | head -1 | cut -d/ -f3 | tr -d '"')
  curl -s -X PUT "localhost:8092/whatif/healthcare/$HID" \
    -d person_id= -d name="Darrell Gallion" -d current_age=67 \
    -d current_coverage=medicare -d current_monthly_cost=650 \
    -d post_medicare_inflation=4.5 | grep -A8 'id="income-removed-toast"'
    # -> visible toast "Removed Rebuild Payroll", unrelated to this action
  scripts/whatif-verify.sh stop 8092

This is in-scope: the `whatif-removed-income-sources` define block was
entirely rewritten by this attempt (git diff HEAD, not `git diff master`,
shows the old per-item permanent list replaced by the toast markup). It is
not a pre-existing defect — the old design (permanent, always-accurate
list, no ephemeral "just happened" framing) did not have this failure
mode.

====================================================================
Items verified PASSING (own live render / Playwright / axe)
====================================================================

1. TOAST STRUCTURE (when triggered by an actual, current-session remove):
   `role="status"`, a real `<button data-income-toast-undo
   hx-post="/whatif/income/{id}/restore">Undo</button>` (focusable, no
   inline onclick), a real `<button data-income-toast-dismiss
   aria-label="Dismiss">` (focusable). Keyboard Esc dismiss verified via
   Playwright (`document.getElementById('income-removed-toast')` gains
   `hidden` on Escape keydown — web/static/js/whatif-income-toast.js:25-29).
   Click-dismiss verified. No inline onclick anywhere in the diff.
   Focus-restoration verified live: after clicking Undo (which OOB-swaps
   the toast holding focus), `document.activeElement` becomes
   `#income-sources-list` (tabindex="-1", per ACCESSIBILITY.md #10) —
   confirmed via Playwright trace of `htmx:oobBeforeSwap`.
   Contrast: toast bg `bg-gray-900 dark:bg-gray-800` / `text-white` —
   very high contrast in both themes; Undo/Dismiss focus rings use
   `focus:ring-accent`, visible in both themes.

2. PERSON CARD:
   - Manual person (both real persons in the isolated data, "Darrell
     Gallion" and "Christine", are unlinked): name renders once (header),
     no "Source:" row, `<div class="col-span-2">` widens the Person
     select to fill the row. Confirmed via live GET.
   - Toggled to linked (`PUT .../healthcare/{id} person_id=<real-person-id>`):
     name still renders once (header shows "You"), the old duplicate
     "Linked Person"/"Derived Age" display cards are gone (hidden inputs
     carry the values in the PUT body instead), and "Source: Linked to
     canonical person" appears exactly when linked. Confirmed via live PUT.
   - `{{.CurrentCoverage.Label}}` still used in the coverage-timeline
     partial (line ~295 of the diff) — not reverted to inline if/else.
   - All `data-quick-adjust-key`/`data-quick-adjust-display` hooks present
     and intact on every slider (grep-verified against the diff).

3. SLIDER VALUE ADJACENCY: every healthcare slider (Monthly Cost, Coverage
   Ends In, Pre/Post-Medicare Inflation, ACA Cost/Inflation, Medicare Cost)
   now renders `<div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
   <label>...</label><span data-quick-adjust-display>...</span></div>`
   immediately above the `<input type=range>` — value is adjacent to its
   own label, not in a separate/distant column. Confirmed by reading the
   live-rendered HTML for both healthcare-person cards.

4. FAB CLEARANCE (Playwright, scrolled to `document.documentElement.
   scrollHeight`, i.e. the true bottom of the page):
   - 1440x900: FAB (`#quick-adjust-toggle`) viewport rect
     top=832 bottom=876; the settings-rail grid's lowest content
     (`#whatif-settings-col`) bottom = 680 (viewport-relative, after
     scrolling to the document's absolute bottom) — clears the FAB by
     152px. The reserved `<div class="hidden lg:block h-28"
     aria-hidden="true">` (112px) is present in the DOM, sized to the
     closed-FAB footprint as documented in the task's own code comment.
   - 390x844: confirmed via `checkVisibility()` that the FAB's ancestor
     (`class="hidden lg:block"`) computes `display:none` and the FAB's
     own `getBoundingClientRect()` collapses to 0 — the FAB is not
     rendered below `lg` (1024px), so the 390 clearance question is moot,
     exactly as the task note anticipated.

5. AXE SWEEP (real Chromium render, axe-core 4.13.0, light + dark via
   `localStorage.theme`, 1440x900 and 390x844, all `<details>` forced
   open): 2 violations in every combination — `label` (28 nodes, e.g.
   `#portfolio-slider`, `#monthly_living_expenses_input`, `person_id`/
   `current_coverage` selects, income-form `start_year`/`end_year`) and
   `select-name` (11 nodes, e.g. `#portfolio-range`, the same
   `current_coverage`/`person_id` selects). Checked `git show
   master:web/templates/components/whatif/healthcare-person.html` — the
   `current_coverage` and `person_id` selects had the identical unlabeled
   structure in master (U13 only changed color-token classes, not the
   label/id structure); the other flagged controls (#portfolio-slider,
   income-form date inputs) are outside every file this attempt touched.
   → PRE-EXISTING, consistent with ruling U-2026-09-03a (U15-scope
   observation), not a U13 FAIL. No NEW violations introduced.
   One unrelated pre-existing contrast finding noted for the backlog: the
   "Add Person" form's selects in `web/templates/components/whatif/
   healthcare-card.html` (untouched by this diff — `git diff` against HEAD
   is empty for that file) render black-on-gray-600 in dark mode
   (ratio 2.78, axe doesn't flag `<select>` native-control contrast) —
   OBSERVATION, out of scope for U13.

6. TOKEN/TYPE FLOOR: `grep -E 'text-\[10px\]|text-\[11px\]'` on the U13
   diff's added lines = 0. No raw hue-literal Tailwind classes
   (`bg-red-*`, `text-blue-*`, etc.) added by this diff — all replaced
   with `text-accent`/`bg-accent-soft`/`text-negative`/`text-positive`/
   `text-warning` tokens, contrast-checked live in both themes (ratios
   5.2–9.4:1, all pass 4.5:1) for the elements this diff actually owns
   (the two real healthcare-person cards' coverage/person selects).

7. Go regression oracle: `TestHandleWhatIfDeleteThenRestoreIncome_Lossless`
   (new, in the diff) drives the real DELETE→POST /restore handlers and
   asserts `reflect.DeepEqual` on every field — a real lossless-round-trip
   check, not just an ID match. Read but not re-run here (that's
   checker-tests' lane); cited for completeness since it's part of the
   diff under audit.

====================================================================
Summary
====================================================================
FAIL on one defect: the Undo-toast rewrite in `whatif-removed-income-
sources` (income-sources-list.html) resurfaces a `role="status"` "Removed
X. Undo" banner for OLD, past-session removed income sources on the very
first (and every subsequent) unrelated what-if mutation, because it always
renders the LAST entry of the persistent `RemovedIncomeSources` list
un-hidden rather than only the item removed by the current action. This
is reproducible from a clean isolated copy of the real production plan
data (which currently holds 5 stale removed-income entries), is squarely
inside this attempt's own new code, and violates both ACCESSIBILITY.md #14
and this task's own "must not resurface" acceptance criterion in the
general (not just page-load) case. Everything else in the U13 diff
(toast structure/keyboard/focus, person-card dedup, slider-adjacent
values, FAB clearance, token floor, axe sweep) verified clean.
